  "treatment": {
    "logline": "A ranch hand watches a drone learn to look for screwworm in brush that hides most of what it needs to find.",
    "cold_open": "Dawn in the Jim Wells County brush. A ranch hand in a palm straw hat shoves into a wall of mesquite, gets stopped, and a drone lifts off the tailgate behind him.",
    "turn": "The detection box sweeps past a bedded deer and finds nothing, then shrinks to a speck under a sky of sterile flies.",
    "button": "The hand walks out to the calf the drone flagged and kneels to look. The drone can point. Somebody still has to look."
  },
  "hero": {
    "name": "the quadcopter with its detection box",
    "why": "it is the machine the story is about and the film follows its box from empty to locked to blind to a speck"
